            <ArticleTitle>[A man with a raised upper arm].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A8279</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 43-year-old man presented at our emergency department with a painful shoulder after a fall with his arm in abduction. Clinical presentation was typical for a luxatio erecta without evidence for neurovasculair damage. It is a rare but important diagnosis because of the high risk of plexus injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
